# Walkthrough: EmbedFS & Hacker UI
## Changes Accomplished
1. Single Binary Deployment (EmbedFS)
We eliminated the dependency on the templates/ folder at runtime.

Before: The server crashed if templates/ was missing.
After: All HTML/CSS files are compiled into embedded_resources.h and built into the binary.
Mechanism: A CMake script (
cmake/GenerateResources.cmake
) converts files to hex strings before compilation. 
ReadOnlyCache
 loads these strings by default.
2. Frontend Redesign (Theme: "Hacker / Cyberpunk")
We replaced the default browser look with a custom dark theme.

Colors: Deep black background (#0d0d0d), Neon Green accents (#00ff41).
Typography: Monospace (Courier New) for that terminal vibe.
Animations: Subtle screen flicker and glow effects.
UX:
"Encrypt & Share" button with status updates.
Result page shows a one-time link that is clearly distinct.

